      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Design first",
      "heading": "Heat loss, flow temperature and MCS 020",
      "html": "<p>A heat pump only works well if the design is right. The record should hold the heat loss basis, the design flow temperature and the outdoor unit siting with its MCS 020 noise check. A low flow temperature keeps the running cost down.</p><p>Quickler asks the installer to confirm the design and photograph the outdoor unit, emitters and cylinder. It does not do the heat loss sum or the noise check. Check the current MCS standards, as they change. This is not regulatory advice.</p>"
